# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Ideovent Technologies — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` for local work. On Netlify set the same names under
# Site configuration → Environment variables. Never commit a filled-in .env —
# `.env` is already in .gitignore.
#
# Step-by-step, including where each value comes from: ../DEPLOY-GUIDE.md
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# ⚠  READ THIS FIRST — WHY NONE OF THESE IS A SECRET
#
# Vite inlines every variable whose name starts with VITE_ into the JavaScript
# bundle at build time. They are shipped to the browser in plain text and anyone
# can read them with View Source. That is normal and expected for the keys
# below — a Supabase anon key and an EmailJS public key are designed to be
# public, and are protected by server-side rules, not by being hidden.
#
# It also means: NEVER put a Supabase service_role key, a database password, a
# Razorpay secret or any private API key in a VITE_ variable. There is no such
# thing as a private variable in this app — it has no server. Anything genuinely
# secret has to live behind a Supabase Edge Function or a Netlify Function.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── 1. SUPABASE — strongly recommended, not optional in practice ─────────────
#
# Without these two the site runs in "local mode", where all content and all
# form submissions are stored in the VISITOR'S OWN BROWSER (localStorage). Read
# that again: a lead submitted from the contact form is written to the sender's
# localStorage, not to anything Mehdi can open. /admin → Submissions on his
# machine will be empty. In local mode EmailJS is the only path a lead has to
# reach anyone. Configure Supabase before taking the site live.
#
# WHERE: supabase.com → your project → Settings → API.
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL      = "Project URL"
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = the "anon / public" key (NOT service_role)
# SETUP: run supabase/migrations/0001_content.sql once in the SQL editor, then
#        create an admin user under Authentication → Users. See SUPABASE_SETUP.md.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# ── 2. ADMIN PASSCODE — local mode only, and NOT a security control ──────────
#
# Used by src/admin/auth.tsx ONLY when Supabase is not configured. Because it is
# a VITE_ variable it is visible in the published bundle, so it keeps out a
# passer-by and nobody else.
#
# When VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are set, this value is
# ignored entirely and /admin requires a real Supabase email + password login.
# That is the only configuration in which the admin is actually protected.
VITE_ADMIN_PASSCODE=change-me-in-local-mode-only


# ── 3. PUBLIC URL — must be set before any certificate is issued ─────────────
#
# src/lib/verify.ts builds certificate QR codes and /verify links from this. If
# it is blank the code falls back to the browser's own origin plus BASE_URL,
# which means a certificate generated on a laptop encodes a localhost URL, and
# one generated from a sub-path build encodes the sub-path.
#
# It must be www, not the apex: every certificate already issued to an intern
# carries a printed QR pointing at www.ideovent.in/verify/<ID>, and printed QR
# codes cannot be recalled. See 13-launchpad/CERTIFICATE-SYSTEM.md §7 Fault 3
# and 03-legal-docs/GUIDE-04-Domain-and-Email-Recovery.md §6.1.
#
# NOTE: as of 24 Sep 2026 this host does not resolve. Setting it here does not
# make it live — the domain has to be registered first (GUIDE-04 §0).
VITE_PUBLIC_URL=https://www.ideovent.in


# ── 4. EMAILJS — delivers the contact form to an inbox ───────────────────────
#
# WHERE: emailjs.com → Email Services (service ID), Email Templates (template
# ID), Account → General (public key).
#
# ⚠ src/components/sections/ContactForm.tsx currently falls back to a hard-coded
#   service ID, template ID and public key if these are unset. Those three
#   values are committed to a public GitHub repository. EmailJS public keys are
#   meant to be public, but an exposed service+template pair can be used by
#   anyone to send mail through that template unless the EmailJS dashboard has
#   its domain allow-list turned on. Before launch: turn on the allow-list for
#   www.ideovent.in, or rotate the service and set the values here.
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=


# ── 5. DEPLOY_BASE — do NOT set this on Netlify or Vercel ────────────────────
#
# Not a VITE_ variable. Read by vite.config.ts to set Vite's `base`. Only the
# GitHub Pages workflow sets it (to /Ideovent-Technologies/), and only because
# Pages serves from a repository sub-path. On a custom domain it must be unset
# so `base` stays "/". Setting it breaks asset URLs, the router basename and the
# origin baked into certificate QR codes.
# DEPLOY_BASE=


# ── 6. NOT USED BY THIS BUILD ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# There is NO Gemini / Google AI key in this repository. The lead-qualifying
# chatbot described in the founder's resume is not present in this source tree —
# grep for "gemini" finds only prose about the Onyx and Aura Orbit case studies.
# If the chatbot is added later, its API key must NOT be a VITE_ variable: it
# would be readable in the bundle and billable by anyone who found it. Put the
# key in a Supabase Edge Function or a Netlify Function and call that.
#
# Razorpay: see section 7 below. /internship still links out to a hosted
# Razorpay payment page (pages.razorpay.com/ideovent).


# ── 7. RAZORPAY: the monthly website plans and the yearly Starter ────────────
#
# Only the KEY ID belongs here, because it is public by design (Razorpay
# Checkout needs it in the browser). Set it ONLY with the LIVE key id
# (rzp_live_...): with it, /pricing shows "Continue to payment"; without it,
# every pay button reads "Pay by UPI or bank transfer on WhatsApp".
#
# The rest are SERVER-ONLY. They go in Vercel's Environment Variables and
# nowhere else, and never with a VITE_ prefix (Vite would print them into the
# public bundle), never in a committed file:
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_ID                 the same key id, read by api/razorpay/*
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET             SECRET
#   RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET         SECRET
#   RAZORPAY_PLAN_STARTER_MONTHLY   plan_... for Rs 899 monthly
#   RAZORPAY_PLAN_GROWTH_MONTHLY    plan_... for Rs 1,999 monthly
#
# Step by step: ../GO-LIVE-IDEOVENT-IN.md, section 10.
VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
